            "detailed_description": "<h1>Language Packs</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game supports <strong>community translations</strong>. Check out <strong>Steam Workshop</strong> to see the available language packs created by other players!</p></p><br><h1>Acerca do jogo</h1>Grey Hack is a massively multiplayer hacking simulator game.<br><br>You're a hacker with full freedom to act as you wish on a vast network of procedurally generated computers.<br><br>File Explorer, Terminal and Text Editor are some of the programs available from the start of the game. As you improve your skills, you'll find new utilities that you can install and use.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/605230/extras/81eabb8e27f21b94eec921d35383ff09.poster.avif?t=1793295994\" width=600 height=336 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/605230/extras/81eabb8e27f21b94eec921d35383ff09.webm?t=1793295994\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/605230/extras/81eabb8e27f21b94eec921d35383ff09.mp4?t=1793295994\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A persistent, living world</h2>Explore the world of Grey Hack and build your own reputation in a world shared by all players. When you leave the game, <strong>the online world stays active 24/7</strong>.<br><br>This ongoing game session means that changes you've made to any computer in the world can be seen by players who connect to it, even when you're no longer online. Your progress will be saved, but your actions can have consequences.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Plan your attacks</h2>Every network in the world has a different configuration, size and level of security. A deep, dynamic exploit system also makes each network and computer a different challenge. Study your target, use social engineering, scan the system for security oversights that could let you open a backdoor, and try different exploits. Above all, cover your tracks when you're done.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Create, modify, share</h2>The terminal plays a fundamental role. Based on real UNIX commands, it is an essential tool for carrying out successful attacks.<br><br>Terminal commands and exploits have been written using the scripting language available in the game. This means you can modify any existing command or create a new one if you wish. You can also create your own exploits if those already available in the world don't meet your needs.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Sandbox</h2>Grey Hack offers a non-linear experience where you progress at your own pace. Publish websites to share your creations, form guilds and organize attacks against other players, complete missions for money and reputation, or explore the world on your own to find hidden special missions and other secrets.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Single-player mode</h2>Grey Hack is designed to be played in multiplayer, benefiting from the richer environment of a world that is always online, but it also offers a single-player mode for those who prefer it. In single-player mode, you play in a world created on your computer. Unlike online mode, when you leave the game, the world stops and progress resumes only when you return.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Roadmap</h2>Grey Hack is currently in beta, version 0.9. You can check the roadmap on the game's Steam forum. I'm open to suggestions: if there's a feature you'd like to see in the game, feel free to let me know through the Steam forums or Discord.",
            "about_the_game": "Grey Hack is a massively multiplayer hacking simulator game.<br><br>You're a hacker with full freedom to act as you wish on a vast network of procedurally generated computers.<br><br>File Explorer, Terminal and Text Editor are some of the programs available from the start of the game. As you improve your skills, you'll find new utilities that you can install and use.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/605230/extras/81eabb8e27f21b94eec921d35383ff09.poster.avif?t=1793295994\" width=600 height=336 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/605230/extras/81eabb8e27f21b94eec921d35383ff09.webm?t=1793295994\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/605230/extras/81eabb8e27f21b94eec921d35383ff09.mp4?t=1793295994\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A persistent, living world</h2>Explore the world of Grey Hack and build your own reputation in a world shared by all players. When you leave the game, <strong>the online world stays active 24/7</strong>.<br><br>This ongoing game session means that changes you've made to any computer in the world can be seen by players who connect to it, even when you're no longer online. Your progress will be saved, but your actions can have consequences.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Plan your attacks</h2>Every network in the world has a different configuration, size and level of security. A deep, dynamic exploit system also makes each network and computer a different challenge. Study your target, use social engineering, scan the system for security oversights that could let you open a backdoor, and try different exploits. Above all, cover your tracks when you're done.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Create, modify, share</h2>The terminal plays a fundamental role. Based on real UNIX commands, it is an essential tool for carrying out successful attacks.<br><br>Terminal commands and exploits have been written using the scripting language available in the game. This means you can modify any existing command or create a new one if you wish. You can also create your own exploits if those already available in the world don't meet your needs.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Sandbox</h2>Grey Hack offers a non-linear experience where you progress at your own pace. Publish websites to share your creations, form guilds and organize attacks against other players, complete missions for money and reputation, or explore the world on your own to find hidden special missions and other secrets.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Single-player mode</h2>Grey Hack is designed to be played in multiplayer, benefiting from the richer environment of a world that is always online, but it also offers a single-player mode for those who prefer it. In single-player mode, you play in a world created on your computer. Unlike online mode, when you leave the game, the world stops and progress resumes only when you return.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Roadmap</h2>Grey Hack is currently in beta, version 0.9. You can check the roadmap on the game's Steam forum. I'm open to suggestions: if there's a feature you'd like to see in the game, feel free to let me know through the Steam forums or Discord.",
